course: dictionary
lesson: 10609
title: Formal words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words sound grown-up and polite, the kind you find in letters and exams. Unduly is one of them. You do not need to be an expert to understand it. Look at the words around it and ask: too much compared with what?
explain: The Badger tells Toad, «don't be unduly anxious». Anxious means worried, and unduly tells you how much worry is meant: more than is needed. The Badger is not saying never worry, only not more than is sensible.
explain: Use the swap check. Put "more than is needed" in place of unduly and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Unduly often comes before words about feelings or actions, as in unduly worried, unduly harsh or not unduly. When you see it, look for the thing that is being done too much.
fact: Unduly is an adverb, a word that tells how much or how something is done.
fact: «Unduly» means more than is right, necessary or reasonable; too much.
fact: Unduly is formal, so you will meet it in polite speech, letters and exams more than in chat.
fact: Phrases to know: unduly worried, unduly harsh, and not unduly, which means not too much.
fact: «Anxious» means worried, so «unduly anxious» means worried more than you need to be.
exercise: «Don't be unduly anxious.» What does unduly tell us? | Very quickly | Happily, with a smile | *More than is needed | Not at all, so never
exercise: The teacher was not unduly harsh after the mistake. What does not unduly harsh mean? | Harsh only at lunchtime | Happy and funny | *Not harsher than is fair | Very cruel and angry
exercise: Which phrase means worried more than is needed? | Kindly worried | *Unduly worried | Quietly worried, like a mouse | Worried in the rain
test: «The referee was not unduly strict, so the game stayed friendly.» What does not unduly strict suggest? | Very silly | Strict in a cruel way | Strict about the football only | *Not stricter than is needed
test: Mum says, «Don't worry unduly about the test.» What should you do? | Worry as much as you can | Cry before you start | Forget the test completely | *Don't worry more than you need to
exam: Which word is the best swap for unduly in «He was not unduly upset by the news»? | *More than is reasonable | Very | Quickly | Happily
